  "interpretation": [
    "Public anonymous visitor_id works from a normal opaque browser frame, but its issued visitor and the documented local encoder did not unlock the tested embedded audio context.",
    "The local encoder had a byte-for-byte synthetic parity control, and the full public context variant also rejected that locally generated identifier.",
    "The SDK clientScreen/Google shape and complete locally generated Session context were tested as code-justified distinct hypotheses; both remained negative.",
    "A single context issued by the neutral public IFrame API example worked for all three separate music IDs, with an invalid-ID negative control. This shows immediate cross-ID reuse on this machine/network, not cross-IP or lifetime validity.",
    "The value came from a fresh public anonymous response with no Cookie, Authorization, user API key or logged-in profile. Its internal fields remain opaque; do not label it an account credential or a stable six-hour guarantee without evidence.",
    "Build-time preparation is distinct from a runtime proxy/server. A static snapshot is now a viable experiment, while automatic mobile bootstrap remains unresolved."
  ],
